<v Dana Chivvis>Here's Dr. Loyd.
<v Dana Chivvis>这是劳埃德医生。

00:37:14.170 --> 00:37:20.740
<v Stephen Loyd>So your training in addiction is on the job from the folks at Express and then the eight-hour X-waiver class?
<v Stephen Loyd>所以你在成瘾方面的培训是在Express的同事那里得到的，然后还有八小时的X-豁免课程？

00:37:20.740 --> 00:37:21.170
<v Michael Lapaglia>Correct.
<v Michael Lapaglia>正确。

00:37:21.170 --> 00:37:22.260
<v Stephen Loyd>OK.
<v Stephen Loyd>好的。

00:37:22.260 --> 00:37:28.800
<v Dana Chivvis>But most of his questions, he's testing LaPaglia, trying to see if he really understands addiction medicine.
<v Dana Chivvis>但他大多数问题都在测试拉帕利亚，试图看他是否真的了解成瘾医学。

00:37:28.800 --> 00:37:35.850
<v Stephen Loyd>Can you tell me how you establish a diagnosis of substance use disorder, severe?
<v Stephen Loyd>你能告诉我你是如何建立重度物质使用障碍诊断的吗？

00:37:35.850 --> 00:37:43.850
<v Michael Lapaglia>Through discussing, taking a drug history, going over medical history with the patient.
<v Michael Lapaglia>通过讨论、记录药物史、与患者一起回顾医疗史。

00:37:43.850 --> 00:37:53.490
<v Stephen Loyd>And so did you ever follow the criteria of the DSM-V for substance use disorder and classifications of mild, moderate, and severe?
<v Stephen Loyd>那么你有没有遵循DSM-V关于物质使用障碍的标准以及轻度、中度、重度的分类？

00:37:53.490 --> 00:37:54.820
<v Michael Lapaglia>No, we didn't put that in the chart.
<v Michael Lapaglia>不，我们没把它放进图表里。

00:37:54.820 --> 00:38:14.640
<v Stephen Loyd>OK, and when you're training-- by way, I 100% agree with you about the prevalence of benzos. That's spot on. But when you're treating benzodiazepine dependence, what is your goal?
<v Stephen Loyd>好的，当你培训时——顺便说一句，我100%同意你关于苯二氮卓类药物流行程度的看法。那很准确。但当治疗苯二氮卓类药物依赖时，你的目标是什么？

00:38:14.640 --> 00:38:16.270
<v Michael Lapaglia>Complete abstinence is the goal.
<v Michael Lapaglia>完全戒断是目标。

00:38:16.270 --> 00:38:19.530
<v Stephen Loyd>OK, and so how do you get there?
<v Stephen Loyd>好的，那你怎么达到那个目标？

00:38:19.530 --> 00:38:21.510
<v Michael Lapaglia>Extremely slowly.
<v Michael Lapaglia>极其缓慢地。

00:38:21.510 --> 00:38:32.160
<v Dana Chivvis>This goes on for several minutes. Dr. Loyd only asks two questions about the L&B scheme itself. When they finally get to deliberations, Dr. Loyd speaks first.
<v Dana Chivvis>这持续了几分钟。劳埃德医生只问了两个关于L&B计划本身的问题。当他们终于开始审议时，劳埃德医生先发言。

00:38:32.160 --> 00:38:53.100
<v Stephen Loyd>I'm the newest member of this committee or this board. And I was told that my charge was to protect the health, safety, and welfare of the citizens of the state of Tennessee. And do I believe that taking Dr. LaPaglia's license does that? I actually don't. I don't believe that it does that.
<v Stephen Loyd>我是这个委员会或这个理事会的新成员。我被告知我的职责是保护田纳西州公民的健康、安全和福祉。我相信吊销拉帕利亚医生的执照能做到这一点吗？我其实不这么认为。我不相信能做到。

00:38:53.100 --> 00:39:08.290
<v Stephen Loyd>From what I saw today, and hopefully, I'm a decent judge of somebody's heart, I saw somebody that cares about taking good care of a population that struggles to find help. That's what I saw.
<v Stephen Loyd>从我今天所看到的，希望我是一个能判断人心的人，我看到的是一个关心照顾那些难以找到帮助的人群的人。那就是我看到的。

00:39:08.290 --> 00:39:19.570
<v Dana Chivvis>One aspect of these medical board hearings that's very different from a criminal trial-- because of transparency laws in Tennessee, the panel members have to deliberate in the open in front of Dr. LaPaglia.
<v Dana Chivvis>这些医疗委员会听证会与刑事审判非常不同的一个方面是——因为田纳西州的透明度法律，小组委员会成员必须在拉帕利亚医生面前公开审议。

00:39:19.570 --> 00:39:36.670
<v Dana Chivvis>Rebecca says this is another reason the discipline can be so light. It's really awkward for them, raises some potential issues. Like at one point, while the panel members are considering requiring Dr. LaPaglia to get board certified in addiction medicine, LaPaglia interrupts them, steers them away from it.
<v Dana Chivvis>丽贝卡说这是纪律处分如此之轻的另一个原因。这对他们来说非常尴尬，引起了一些潜在的问题。比如在某个时候，当小组委员会成员考虑要求拉帕利亚医生获得成瘾医学的委员会认证时，拉帕利亚打断了他们，把他们从这个方向引开。

00:39:36.670 --> 00:39:42.640
<v Woman>Do we want to require him to do that, and if he doesn't complete--
